# Cloudflare Workers Bindings (Archestimator)

Archestimator is **Cloudflare-first**. Don't default to hybrid recommendations. Plan runtime work around Workers/OpenNext, D1, Better Auth, R2, Queues/Cron, Durable Objects/WebSockets, KV-only-safe-cache, Email, WAF/rate-limiting/DDoS, Turnstile where in scope, Web Analytics, Workers Observability.

## Active Bindings

`wrangler.jsonc` is the executable source for binding names, resource names,
classes, queues, routes, and cron triggers. Read it immediately before changing
provider configuration; do not rely on copied inventories in this adapter.

## Worker Env Types

Generated types from `wrangler.jsonc` via `bun run cf:typegen`. Output: `cloudflare-env.d.ts`. **Regenerate after every binding change.** Never hand-edit `cloudflare-env.d.ts`.

## Commands

```bash
bun run cf:typegen                    # regenerate cloudflare-env.d.ts
bun run cf:build                      # opennextjs-cloudflare build
bun run cf:preview                    # build + wrangler preview (local bindings)
bun run cf:deploy                     # EXTERNAL DEPLOY: explicit current-task authorization required
bun run cf:check-readiness            # Worker readiness gate
bun run cf:check-provider             # Cloudflare provider readiness
bun run cf:check-email                # Cloudflare Email readiness
bun run cf:check-dns-delegation       # archestimator.com DNS gate
bun run cf:queues-cron-proof          # Queue + cron proof
bun run cf:better-auth-proof          # Better Auth on D1 proof
bun run cf:d1-runtime-proof           # D1 runtime performance proof
bun run cf:d1-restore-rehearsal       # D1 restore dry-run
bun run cf:provider-exit-pack         # legacy provider-exit evidence
bun run cf:release-gates              # release-gate suite
bun run cf:inventory                  # Cloudflare migration inventory
```

## Local D1

Apply migrations to local preview DB:
```bash
wrangler d1 migrations apply ARCH_DB --local
```

## Durable Objects (`COLLAB_ROOMS`)

Class `CollaborationRoom`. SQLite-backed (Durable Object storage). Broadcasts:

- Cursor positions (estimate sheet editor)
- User presence (project dashboard)
- Sheet-level mutations (realtime sync)

WebSocket connection per room. State persisted in DO storage. See `src/lib/collaboration/` and `src/hooks/use-estimate-cursor-broadcast.ts`, `src/hooks/use-project-presence.ts`.

## Queues (`UPLOAD_JOBS_QUEUE`)

Background jobs for: PDF/XLS upload processing, image processing, async export. Consumer: defined in Worker. DLQ for failed jobs (max 3 retries).

## Cloudflare Email (`EMAIL`)

Transactional email (replaces Resend). See `src/lib/email/cloudflare-email-client.ts`, `src/lib/email/transactional-email-client.ts`. Used for: magic links, invite delivery, publication notifications.

## Cloudflare Images (`IMAGES`)

Component library images, project cover images. See `src/app/api/component-library/images/`, `src/app/api/projects/images/`. Stored via Images binding; fallback to R2 for variants/attachments.

## Cost Posture

Stay on **free-tier / bundled** Cloudflare limits. Do NOT enable paid add-ons without explicit owner approval:
- D1 paid plan
- R2 paid tier
- Workers Smart Placement paid
- Workers Analytics paid
- Dedicated egress

Rely on daily D1 backups + `bun run cf:d1-restore-rehearsal` for the cheaper recovery path.

## Standing Authorization Scope

Philip grants standing authorization for local repository changes inside
resources currently bound in `wrangler.jsonc`. Derive the complete current
binding list from that file. Actual deployment remains separately authorized.

**Out of scope (never touch):**
- Historical Supabase project `ebxxqidacheyapmmzavr`
- The unrelated `archestimator` Cloudflare provider project
- Other Cloudflare accounts
- Other Cloudflare Workers/projects outside `wrangler.jsonc` bindings

## Workers Logs (Production Observability)

`wrangler.jsonc` enables **persisted Workers Logs at full sampling** with traces disabled to preserve shared log quota. For hosted debugging, use Cloudflare Workers Logs / Real-time logs or `wrangler tail` as production evidence. Local logs (`logs/dev.ndjson`) are NOT hosted proof.

## Cache Components + KV

Workers KV can be used as a safe cache layer when:

- Cache key includes privacy scope (workspace/user where relevant)
- TTL bounded
- Read-your-own-writes handled via cache tag invalidation

Don't use KV as primary store. Use D1 for primary, KV for cache.

## OpenNext Adapter

`@opennextjs/cloudflare` ^1.20.1 is the active adapter. Build: `bun run cf:build` runs `opennextjs-cloudflare build`. Output deploys to Worker. Read `open-next.config.*` before changing adapter behavior.

## Forbidden

- Mutating Cloudflare resources outside `wrangler.jsonc` bindings
- Enabling paid add-ons without explicit owner approval
- Hardcoding binding names that diverge from `wrangler.jsonc`
- Editing `cloudflare-env.d.ts` manually (regenerate via `cf:typegen`)
- Defaulting to hybrid recommendations (this is Cloudflare-first)
